summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The board identified a preferred candidate and voted unanimously to authorize the chair to enter negotiations; the candidate's name was not disclosed while talks are pending.
- topic: Top Scholars Recognition
  text: Eighteen Class of 2026 top scholars were honored in a student-led ceremony, with valedictorian Alexander Davison and salutatorian Audrey LeBleu introducing one another at the podium.
- topic: FY2026 Budget Outlook
  text: Finance Director Abigail Kitchen reported a year-end range from a $10,000 surplus to a $2.09 million deficit; city council voted to offer up to $2 million in debt forgiveness.
- topic: MaineCare Billing
  text: Director of Instructional Support Kat Cox outlined the district's existing billing process (OT, speech, PT) and two potential expansions, with cautions about audit risk and documentation burden.
- topic: Elementary Reconfiguration
  text: A 23-member steering committee was announced to guide the Kaler Elementary closure process; a parent survey on student placement preferences was sent the same day.
- topic: Educational Equity Policy
  text: The board took a first read on a new equity policy developed by the DEI director and equity committee, alongside a first read of the updated agenda policy (BEDB).
- topic: Bus Safety
  text: A parent and transportation employee raised urgent concerns about chronic overcrowding on buses during spring track meets; the superintendent committed to investigate and the board requested a June status report.
